    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "This is correct.\nCombination chemotherapy offers potentially curative therapy for DLBCL, regardless of the stage. The addition of the anti-CD20 antibody rituximab to cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin, vincristine, and prednisone (R-CHOP) improved survival beyond CHOP alone and is the standard first-line chemotherapy for this disease. For patients with early-stage disease localized to a radiation field, treatment options include full course chemotherapy with R-CHOP every 3 weeks for 6 cycles, or abbreviated chemotherapy for 3-4 cycles followed by involved field radiotherapy. For advanced stage DLBCL, therapy is with a full course of chemotherapy.",
