    "id": "notion-internal-medicine-0036",
    "subject": "internal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 36,
    "stem": "Which of the following may prevent anal condylomas?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Application of liquid nitrogen"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Intralesional interferon alpha"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Vaccination with EPV vaccine"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Application of podophyllotoxin"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Human Papillomavirus (HPV) vaccines, such as the HPV vaccine, are preventive measures against certain strains of HPV, which is the primary cause of anal condylomas. The vaccine is effective in preventing infection with specific high-risk HPV types that are associated with genital warts and cervical cancer. Vaccination is considered a key strategy in reducing the incidence of anal condylomas.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Liquid nitrogen is commonly used in cryotherapy to freeze and destroy abnormal tissues, including anal condylomas (genital warts). It works by causing freezing injury to the treated tissue, leading to necrosis and subsequent shedding of the wart. While cryotherapy can be effective in removing existing condylomas, it is primarily a treatment rather than a preventive measure.",
      "B": "Intralesional interferon alpha is a form of immunotherapy that involves injecting interferon directly into the affected tissue. Interferon is a signaling protein that plays a role in the body's immune response. While it may be used to treat anal condylomas, it is not a preventive measure. It works by modulating the immune system's response to the viral infection.",
      "C": "Human Papillomavirus (HPV) vaccines, such as the HPV vaccine, are preventive measures against certain strains of HPV, which is the primary cause of anal condylomas. The vaccine is effective in preventing infection with specific high-risk HPV types that are associated with genital warts and cervical cancer. Vaccination is considered a key strategy in reducing the incidence of anal condylomas.",
      "D": "Podophyllotoxin is a topical treatment used to destroy genital warts, including anal condylomas. Similar to cryotherapy, it is a therapeutic intervention rather than a preventive measure. It works by interfering with the growth of the wart tissue."
    },
