    "id": "notion-internal-medicine-0056",
    "subject": "internal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 56,
    "stem": "Situation 6- Janilyn, 30 years old asthmatic uncontrolled by LABA and SABA has been taking glucocorticoids for nearly a year. She started experiencing severe low back pains which she attributed to her weight gain. She also complains of occasional abdominal pains; You wanted to rule out spine fracture based on the given history. Which test (s) will you request for?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "CT scan of cervicothoracic spines"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "X-ray of thoracolumbar spines"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "PET scan"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Bone densitometry"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "X-rays are commonly used to assess bone structures, and they can be useful in detecting fractures, dislocations, or other abnormalities in the spine. An X-ray of the thoracolumbar spines is a reasonable initial imaging test to evaluate for fractures, especially if there are concerns about potential trauma or injury.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "A CT scan is a detailed imaging modality that provides cross-sectional images of the spine. It is particularly useful for assessing bony structures and detecting fractures. If there is suspicion of spine fracture, a CT scan of the cervicothoracic spines may help visualize the region and identify any fractures or abnormalities.",
      "B": "X-rays are commonly used to assess bone structures, and they can be useful in detecting fractures, dislocations, or other abnormalities in the spine. An X-ray of the thoracolumbar spines is a reasonable initial imaging test to evaluate for fractures, especially if there are concerns about potential trauma or injury.",
      "C": "Positron Emission Tomography (PET) scans are not typically used as a primary imaging modality for detecting spine fractures. PET scans are more commonly employed in assessing metabolic activity in tissues and are useful for detecting certain types of cancers and other conditions.",
      "D": "Bone densitometry, often done through Dual-Energy X-ray Absorptiometry (DEXA) scans, is primarily used to assess bone mineral density and is commonly employed in the diagnosis and management of osteoporosis. While it is not the primary test for detecting fractures, it provides valuable information about bone health."
    },
