    "id": "notion-internal-medicine-0058",
    "subject": "internal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 58,
    "stem": "Management of miss Janilyn’s osteoporosis includes the following EXCEPT:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Risk factor reduction"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Fall prevention strategies"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Institution of oral calcium and vitamin"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Administration of contraceptive pill"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "The administration of contraceptive pills is not a standard treatment for osteoporosis. While certain hormonal medications may have bone-protective effects, contraceptive pills are primarily used for birth control and hormonal regulation. The choice of osteoporosis management typically involves medications specifically designed to enhance bone density and reduce the risk of fractures.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Risk factor reduction is a crucial component of osteoporosis management. This may involve addressing modifiable risk factors such as smoking cessation, reducing alcohol intake, and maintaining a healthy lifestyle. Identifying and addressing risk factors help in preventing further bone loss and fractures.",
      "B": "Fall prevention is essential in osteoporosis management, especially in elderly individuals who are at an increased risk of fractures due to falls. This includes strategies such as improving home safety, balance exercises, and addressing factors that may contribute to falls.",
      "C": "Calcium and vitamin D are essential for bone health. Adequate calcium intake, along with vitamin D, is crucial for maintaining bone density and preventing further bone loss. Oral supplementation is often recommended, particularly if dietary intake is insufficient.",
      "D": "The administration of contraceptive pills is not a standard treatment for osteoporosis. While certain hormonal medications may have bone-protective effects, contraceptive pills are primarily used for birth control and hormonal regulation. The choice of osteoporosis management typically involves medications specifically designed to enhance bone density and reduce the risk of fractures."
    },
