    "id": "notion-internal-medicine-0094",
    "subject": "internal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 94,
    "stem": "While explaining to his family the pathology of his illness, you mention the more common causes of his illness namely:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Hyperlipidemia"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Alcohol intake"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Blunt trauma"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Drug intake"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Alcohol Intake is the 2nd most common cause of acute pancreatitis. Excessive alcohol consumption can lead to inflammation of the pancreas. Chronic alcohol abuse is a well-established risk factor for developing pancreatitis.\nGallstone is the most common cause of acute pancreatitis worldwide.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Hyperlipidemia is a known risk factor for acute pancreatitis. Elevated levels of triglycerides, a type of blood fat, can lead to the development of pancreatitis. It is particularly relevant in cases of severe hypertriglyceridemia.",
      "B": "Alcohol Intake is the 2nd most common cause of acute pancreatitis. Excessive alcohol consumption can lead to inflammation of the pancreas. Chronic alcohol abuse is a well-established risk factor for developing pancreatitis.\nGallstone is the most common cause of acute pancreatitis worldwide.",
      "C": "Blunt Trauma to the abdomen can also cause acute pancreatitis, although it is less common. Injury to the pancreas, such as from a motor vehicle accident or a fall, can trigger inflammation.",
      "D": "Drug Intake can contribute to acute pancreatitis, although it is less common. Certain medications, such as certain antibiotics, immunosuppressants, and diuretics, have been associated with pancreatitis."
    },
