    "id": "superexam-internal-medicine-0142",
    "subject": "internal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 142,
    "stem": "You are treating a case of sepsis in which the culture\nand sensitivity results are still unavailable, the\npractice of giving antibiotics before C & S becomes\navailable is defined as",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Giving an antibiotic which has a broad spectrum\nof activity without knowing the specific organism"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Withholding the treatment while awaiting C & S\nresults"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Tailoring the antibiotic regimen guided by the\nresults from the culture and sensitivity"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Both A and C"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "None of the above"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "Empiric therapy is giving the antibiotic treatment\nwith broad spectrum of activity for a suspected\norganism/s without the benefit of knowing the\nsusceptibility patterns of such organism/s. Once\nthe results of the C &S become available, the\ntherapy can then be tailored depending on the\nsusceptibility results.",
