    "id": "superexam-internal-medicine-0428",
    "subject": "internal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 428,
    "stem": "Which of the following statements about insulin\nsynthesis and secretion is not true?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Blood glucose level of >70 mg/dl stimulates\ninsulin synthesis."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Glucose phosphorylation by glucokinase is the\nrate-limiting step in glucose-regulated insulin\nsecretion."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Glucose is transported to the pancreatic beta\ncells by an active glucose transport."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "All of the above"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "None of the above"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Glucose stimulation of insulin secretion starts with\nentry of glucose molecules into pancreatic beta\ncells by means of a facilitative glucose transporter\n(GLUT 2). Options A and B are true. (HPIM, DM\nChapter 18th edition)",
