    "id": "superexam-internal-medicine-0432",
    "subject": "internal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 432,
    "stem": "The best way to confirm the diagnosis of aortic\nstenosis is by performing:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "An electrocardiogram"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "An echocardiogram"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "An exercise stress test"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "A radionuclide ventriculogram"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Echo study with Doppler can detect the valvular\nproblem, quantify its severity and assess left\nventricular function. Although a ventriculogram\ncan tell about ventricular function, it cannot assess\ndisease severity. ECG is non-specific whereas a\nstress test is contraindicated in symptomatic\npatients.",
