    "id": "superexam-internal-medicine-0600",
    "subject": "internal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 600,
    "stem": "The pathophysiology of which disease CANNOT be\nexplain by the Hygiene Hypothesis?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "AIDS"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Allergy"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Asthma"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Autoimmunde disease"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "ALL"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "AIDS is an infection and cannot be explain by the\nhygiene hypothesis. The hygiene hypothesis states\nthat a lack of early childhood exposure to\ninfectious agents, symbiotic microorganisms, and\nparasites increases susceptibility to allergic\ndiseases by suppressing natural development of\nthe immune system.",
