    "id": "superexam-internal-medicine-0613",
    "subject": "internal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 613,
    "stem": "A patient with complete biliary obstruction\ndeveloped bleeding tendencies. Which of the\nfollowing parameters may be prolonged?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Partial thromboplastin time"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Prothrombin time"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Bleeding time"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "All of the above"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "A and B"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "E",
    "explanation": "Patients with complete biliary obstruction will\nhave impaired absorption of fat-soluble vitamins,\none of which is vitamin K. It is expected in this\npatient that his PTT and PT may be prolonged, due\nto inadequate amounts of factors 10, 9, 7 and 2.\nFactor 10 and 2 is part of both intrnsic and\nextrinsic coagulation pathway (common pathway),\nsuch that both PTT and PT may be affected.",
